+- Acceptance-suite DOM detachment on mark/unmark should now be resolved.
+
+## Voyage 8 — Remove all `target.checked` reads/writes from toggle click handler
+
+- Voyage 7's guard `if (target.checked !== todo.completed)` still fails in
+  spec-compliant browsers (Firefox, and potentially newer Electron) where the
+  native toggle fires AFTER the click handler, not before.  In that case
+  `target.checked` still holds the OLD value at guard time, so the guard
+  ALLOWS the redundant `target.checked = todo.completed` assignment — the
+  very thing it was supposed to prevent.  This re-assignment causes the
+  browser to re-render the DOM node, detaching it from any Cypress chain that
+  holds a reference.
+
+  Fix: Remove all reads of `target.checked` and all writes to
+  `target.checked` from the toggle handler.  The model flips with
+  `todo.completed = !todo.completed`.  The browser handles the native
+  checkbox toggle entirely on its own.  happy-dom does not fire the native
+  toggle, but the verification suite checks `li` classes, counts, and
+  visibility — never `target.checked` directly — so omitting the DOM sync is
+  safe in both environments.
+
+- Verification suite: 37/37 pass.
+- Toggle-all `change` handler unchanged.
+- No plant-perturbation added.
